  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Read H10DataverseAppUserGraphParityHandler.cs's existing implementation + its existing tests in full.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Confirm grants">Verify task 111's Grant-ControlPlaneIdentity.ps1 has run successfully against the target environment's tenant (the C5.8 grants exist).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Live invocation">Invoke H10 against a real dev target (a freshly-created env from task 140, or the existing dev stamp) and observe each of the 5 seams' outcome.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Verify App User creation">Confirm the customer UAMI AND the BFF app-reg both resolve as Dataverse App Users post-invocation.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Verify Graph parity">Confirm Graph app-role assignments match GraphAppRoles.cs's completed catalog (11 of 14 -- verify the parity check correctly reports the 3 still-null entries as a known gap, not a false pass).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Report">File a verification report in notes/ documenting each seam's live outcome, any deviation found, and confirmation that the existing test suite's assertions match live behavior.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If ANY of the 5 seams fails live verification, STOP and escalate — do not silently mark this task complete with a partial pass. DS-4's classification of H10 as fully real makes ANY live failure noteworthy: it either means task 111's grants are incomplete/wrong, or DS-4's classification itself needs correction, both of which require a decision, not a workaround.</trigger>
